Technical Specification: AWS & GitLab OIDC Integration

1. Overview
This document outlines the procedure for establishing a secure, passwordless authentication flow between GitLab CI/CD and AWS using OpenID Connect (OIDC). This method eliminates the need for long-lived AWS IAM Access Keys.

2. AWS Setup
2.1 Identity Provider (IdP)
Navigate to IAM > Identity Providers.

Click Add provider and select OpenID Connect.

Provider URL: https://gitlab.com

Audience: https://gitlab.com

Click Get thumbprint and save.

2.2 IAM Role Trust Policy
Create a new IAM Role. Use the following Trust Relationship to restrict access to your specific GitLab project and branch:

JSON
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:oidc-provider/gitlab.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
      "Condition": {
        "StringLike": {
          "gitlab.com:sub": "project_path:YOUR_ORG/YOUR_REPO:ref_type:branch:ref:main"
        },
        "StringEquals": {
          "gitlab.com:aud": "https://gitlab.com"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

3. GitLab Configuration
3.1 CI/CD Variables
Navigate to Settings > CI/CD > Variables and add:

Key: ROLE_ARN

Value: arn:aws:iam::YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:role/YOUR_ROLE_NAME

3.2 Pipeline Script (.gitlab-ci.yml)
Use the following configuration to authorize the runner:

YAML
image: 
  name: amazon/aws-cli:latest
  entrypoint: [""]

variables:
  AWS_DEFAULT_REGION: us-east-1
  AWS_PROFILE: oidc

before_script:
  - mkdir -p ~/.aws
  - echo "${CI_JOB_JWT_V2}" > /tmp/web_identity_token
  - echo -e "[profile oidc]\nrole_arn = ${ROLE_ARN}\nweb_identity_token_file = /tmp/web_identity_token" > ~/.aws/config

validate_connection:
  script:
    - aws sts get-caller-identity
    - aws s3 ls
4. Security Benefits
No Secret Management: No AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID or AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY stored in GitLab.

Short-lived Credentials: Tokens expire automatically after the job finishes.

Granular Access: Permissions are scoped down to the specific repository and branch level.
